The attached image illustrates that Nano-11 facilitates the transport of antigens to lymph nodes. Flow cytometry plots and corresponding bar graphs demonstrate that Nano-11, when co-administered with ovalbumin (OVA), leads to a significantly higher mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA in antigen-presenting cells (APCs) within the draining lymph nodes on both day 1 and day 2 compared to OVA alone or with aluminum hydroxide (AH). Furthermore, Nano-11 increases the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among the OVA-positive cells, indicating enhanced antigen delivery to these key immunopotentiating cells. This highlights Nano-11's superior efficiency in antigen uptake and targeting to MigDCs compared to conventional adjuvants.